{"answers":[{"question_id":"Q014_paper_example_reclassification_pa1492","answer":"In SCOP 1.69, PA1492 (1t1j chain A, domain d1t1ja_, sunid 106249) was not related to nucleoside 2-deoxyribosyltransferase (1f8y, d1f8ya_) at any level below class. PA1492 sat in its own one-member fold, c.137 (sccs c.137.1.1, superfamily c.137.1 'Hypothetical protein PA1492'), while 1f8y sat in c.23 (Flavodoxin-like), superfamily c.23.14, family c.23.14.1. Both were only in class c (alpha and beta proteins), so the two were classified as unrelated folds.

In the current release (2.08), the same domain sunid 106249 is now d1t1ja1 (chain-level naming changed from d1t1ja_ to d1t1ja1; the SCCS is c.23.14.2) and is placed in superfamily c.23.14 with 1f8y's family c.23.14.1. So the change is that PA1492 moved from a different fold (c.137 vs c.23) into the same fold and superfamily as nucleoside 2-deoxyribosyltransferase, as a new family, c.23.14.2 'Hypothetical protein PA1492'. The two now share fold c.23 and superfamily c.23.14, which SCOPe treats as evidence of common evolutionary origin (homology at the superfamily level). They are still different families (c.23.14.1 vs c.23.14.2), so family-level homology is not claimed.

Limits: (1) The 2.08 superfamily name for c.23.14 changed from 'N-deoxyribosyltransferase' (1.69) to 'N-(deoxy)ribosyltransferase-like'; the SCCS did not change, so that is a label change, not a reclassification. (2) The tools confirm the before and after placements but not the curators' reasoning; the sequence and structure evidence behind the move was not checked here. Sequence identity, FATCAT hits and the Andreeva et al. 2008 text were not consulted, so I cannot say what that paper concluded beyond these SCOPe records. (3) A superfamily-level placement is a classification statement, not proof of shared function or transferable annotation. PA1492 is annotated as a structural genomics target with no function transfer implied. (4) The 1.69 search_scop call failed (search index not initialized), so the 1.69 PA1492 placement comes from the PDB-entry, chain and node records, not from search.","evidence_used":["mcp__scope__get_scop_service_info","mcp__scope__get_scop_domains","mcp__scope__search_scop","mcp__scope__get_scop_pdb_entry","mcp__scope__get_scop_chain","mcp__scope__get_scop_node","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1t1ja1","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1t1ja1/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1t1ja1/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1f8ya_/parents","/api/v1/releases/1.69/sids/d1f8ya_/parents","/api/v1/releases/1.69/pdb/1t1j/domains","/api/v1/releases/1.69/chains/1t1jA","/api/v1/releases/1.69/sccs/c.137.1/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=PA1492"]}]}
